    21	resource limiters) runs only after the review in
    22	[docs/runbooks/compute-flags.md](docs/runbooks/compute-flags.md): its memory and
    23	time limits, threads, environment and every flag checked against the tool's
    24	own help, starting from the best measured combination in that runbook's table
    25	and adding or superseding a row after the run.
    26	
    27	**Pull requests and the audit.** The workflow `pr.yml` runs
    28	`sh ci/pr_checks.sh lint|types|tests|gates` on every pull request push: Ruff
    29	and mypy over ci/, tests/, gororoba_quantum/, scripts/ and kaggle_kernel/,
    30	pytest over tests/ with `-m "not audit"`, and the ci/gates.json gates of at
    31	most 15 measured seconds that the diff from main reaches (a record binding an
    32	edited producer's digest fails there). Branch protection on main requires
    33	the four checks `lint`, `types`, `tests` and `gates` green on the head; with the Codex
    34	review loop they admit a merge ([Merging](#reviews-and-merges)), and no local
    35	gate run or premerge replay is required. Locally, `sh ci/pr_checks.sh tests
    36	PATH` runs the touched tests under the hosted environment; pushing needs no
    37	exhaustive run. `ci.yml` is the audit: every gate, the retained-evidence
    38	replays, the Rocq replays and the ledger, nightly on main and on manual
    39	dispatch ([ci/AGENTS.md](ci/AGENTS.md)). A failing scheduled run updates the
    40	issue "Nightly audit failing" with each failing gate and the claims citing it;
    41	it blocks no unrelated pull request.
    42	
    43	**Code style.** Every Python file a change touches passes, before each push,
    44	through `"$PYTHON" ci/pinned_tool.py TOOL ARGS` (the versions of
    45	ci/requirements-ci.txt):
    46	- `ruff format --target-version py313` (120-column lines from pyproject.toml;
    47	  the Python 3.13 target is the Quantum Inspire interpreter's);
    48	- `ruff check` (pycodestyle, pyflakes, import order, bugbear, pyupgrade, S101);
    49	- `mypy` on the touched files, and over gororoba_quantum/, scripts/, ci/,
    50	  tests/ and kaggle_kernel/ (from gororoba_quantum/: `mypy . ../scripts ../ci
    51	  ../tests ../kaggle_kernel`) when a change alters a signature another module
