   101	other integer; the run record's `seed_source` names the spelling, and the
   102	change that retains a qrng-seeded run adds its ledger row with
   103	`"$PYTHON" ci/seed_provenance.py --add-runtime`.
   104	
   105	## Work planning
   106	
   107	[docs/state/plans.md](docs/state/plans.md) is the planning entry point. JSON records own work status;
   108	Markdown views are generated. Capture ideas cheaply, then record scope, owner, next action and checkable
   109	steps before committing work. Update records when scope changes, work pauses or an obligation closes.
   110	Completion requires scope-bound receipts; scientific claims and provider approvals keep their existing
   111	authorities. Reconcile JSON conflicts by hand, regenerate views and run `scripts/plan_tracker.py check`.
   112	The [operator procedure](docs/runbooks/plan-tracker.md) documents commands and shared-checkout locking.
   113	
   114	## Source library and research replay
   115	
   116	`docs/` owns source notes, retained PDFs, retrieval identities and research
   117	replays, and [docs/README.md](docs/README.md) is the map of every document.
   118	`literature -> docs` preserves recorded paths; new Markdown links use `docs/`. Immutable source ledgers retain their recorded bytes. External-only sources (`redistribution: excluded_without_permission`) keep their reading copies and Markdown transcriptions in the owner's private repository
   119	[gororoba-quantum-documents](https://github.com/Oichkatzelesfrettschen/gororoba-quantum-documents), cloned beside this checkout; `"$PYTHON" scripts/fetch_source_cache.py --missing --from-documents DIR` restores the
   120	ignored `docs/local_source_cache/` from it, and the same command without `--from-documents` fetches the registered URLs.
   121	Only that repository receives those files; [docs/sources/reading-copies.md](docs/sources/reading-copies.md), regenerated by `scripts/source_reading_copies.py` after every registry change, links each one beside its public source. The
   122	`sources` suite in ci/gates.json covers the source registry, the evidence
   123	replays and their checksum ledgers.
   124	
   125	
   126	Changes to proof replay inputs also follow the pinned Rocq replay in
   127	`docs/evidence/folding_proofs/README.md`. Imported paper parser diagnostics
   128	remain source limitations in the registry; checksum admission preserves the
   129	original bytes and differs from a fresh mathematical proof check.
   130	
   131	**Computer algebra.** Exact replays compute in global monomial orderings (`dp`,
   132	`lp`). A local invariant at a point p, such as a tangent cone, multiplicity or
   133	singularity type, comes from the deformation to the normal cone: translate p
   134	to 0, substitute t -> h t, take `sat(I, h)` (an ideal in Singular 4.4, not a
   135	list) and set h = 0. The reduced germ at p is the intersection of the
   136	`minAssGTZ` primes through p, with no prior `radical()`. Local orderings (`ds`,
   137	`tangentcone`) on the A_5 strata ran past an hour at tens of GiB on the shared
   138	host, while the global route takes seconds
   139	([a5-strata-regularity](docs/evidence/a5-strata-regularity/README.md)). A
   140	long Singular or msolve run follows the flag review above.
   141	
   142	## Documents
   143	
   144	[docs/README.md](docs/README.md) is the map and decides where a document
   145	lives; read it before writing one.
   146	
   147	- Extend before adding. A fact has one home; a second area that needs it gets
   148	  a link, and a deduplication merges the fact up to the nearest home every
   149	  reader reaches, never into sibling copies.
   150	- Place by kind: a source note in `docs/notes/papers/` with its
   151	  `docs/SOURCES.json` record; a research note in `docs/notes/topics/`; a
   152	  provider guide in `docs/notes/<provider>/`; a design or plan in
   153	  `docs/design/`; operator commands in `docs/runbooks/`; a replay and its
   154	  retained output in `docs/evidence/<name>/`; generated registries in
   155	  `docs/state/`; handoffs, session logs and review reports in
   156	  `docs/archive/`. Session-local scratch stays in the ignored `docs/local/`.
   157	- A new document gets its map row or an inbound link in the same change;
   158	  `scripts/check_markdown_links.py` fails on a broken link or anchor.
   159	- Names state target and mechanism in lowercase with hyphens; a date or
   160	  phase label appears only under `docs/archive/`.
   161	- Retained bytes are immutable: a file a ledger, record or digest binds keeps
   162	  its path and bytes, and a correction lands in a new document that the old
   163	  one's map row links.
   164	- A move runs through `git mv` and updates every reference, ledger and gate
   165	  in the same change.
   166	- An AGENTS.md holds rules a session cannot derive from the tree, kept short;
   167	  reference tables, procedures and measurements live in the docs they
   168	  describe, with a pointer.
   169	
