     1	# First-principles plan for the four failed A_5 fiber runs
     2	
     3	Tags: [F] file (path:line), [M] measured by me (probes/, Singular 4.4.1, p=32009, nice, 2 GiB cap, host at load 36), [I] inferred.
     4	Purpose (purpose.md): the exceptional fiber Proj F(I), F(I)=sum I^d/mI^d, of Y blown up along Z; deliver dim, degree, Hilbert function, components.
     5	
     6	## 1. What each run computes and where it breaks
     7	Common object [F inputs/e8_np_fiber.sing, kaggle xp_np/input.sing:5-15]: A=k[t]/J (7 slice variables, germ dim 4, X to N), I=(G), s=15 generators. h_d=dim F_d. Degree d relations K_d = {c : sum c_b P_b in mP_d+J}. Scripts take syz(U_d) of ~960 columns in the LOCAL ring ds.
     8	- xp_np: h2=51 took 25470 s (xp_np/singular.log:4) because 3 jobs shared 4 vCPU and syz in ds tracks 961 components. It died in the degree-3 syz [F singular.log "no more memory", Appl 12.3 GB] against RLIMIT_AS=12 GiB [F kernel_run.py as_bytes 12884901888]. RSS peaked 6.7 GiB while MemAvailable was 22 GiB [F samples.tsv t=25665]. Cap-bound, not RAM-bound; also time-heavy.
     9	- xm_nm: degree 2 only (no K3 in input.sing). Finished std: 69 relations, projdim 3, degree 12, then minAssGTZ ran 15,600 s at 4 GB RSS (time-bound, flat RSS in samples.tsv). Its result is V(K2), a superset of the fiber.
    10	- iso_k2: K2 (68 quadrics, 17 vars) std instant; minAssGTZ ran 40,000 s at 1 GB (time-bound).
    11	- E8 msolve: 31 variables (a,t1..t9,y1..y21), 37 equations y_i-a*G_i plus J [F e8_np.ms]. The last log line `7 407116 432548` is deg/sel/pairs, not a matrix: degree 7 selects 407,116 pairs (all of the minimal degree) [F e8_np_msolve_solo.log tail], versus 6,075 at degree 6 with matrix 206843x468377. Row count jumps 67x and the monomial table doubles to 2^28. Solo death had MemAvailable 51 GB at RSS 33.6 GB [F solo.samples.tsv], so the address-space cap killed it; but all variants die at the same step, so 2^28 slots at ~30+ virtual bytes each (about 40 GiB with the old block live during realloc) [I] is real demand.
    12	- w8_nm: 24 generators, 325 products, 2,600 syz columns, died at 83 GB RSS before h2 (RSS rose steadily, memory-bound) [F w8_nm_fiber.samples.tsv].
