  1338	  Description
  1339	   Text
  1340	     Let $M$ be an $R = k[x_1,\ldots,x_n]/J$-module (for example an ideal), and
  1341	     let $mm=ideal vars R = (x_1,\ldots,x_n)$, and suppose that $M$ is a
  1342	     homomorphic image of the free module $F$. Let $T$ be the Rees algebra of
  1343	     $M$. The call specialFiberIdeal(M) returns the ideal $J\subset{} Sym(F)$
  1344	     such that $Sym(F)/J \cong{} T/mm*T$; that is, $specialFiberIdeal(M) =
  1345	     reesIdeal(M)+mm*Sym(F).$
  1346	
  1347	     The name derives from the fact that $Proj(T/mm*T)$ is the special fiber of
  1348	     the blowup of $Spec R$ along the subscheme defined by $I$.
  1349	     
  1350	     With the default Trim => true, the computation begins by computing minimal generators,
  1351	     which may result in a change of generators of M
  1352	   Example
  1353	     R=QQ[a..h]
  1354	     M=matrix{{a,b,c,d},{e,f,g,h}}
  1355	     analyticSpread minors(2,M)
  1356	     specialFiberIdeal minors(2,M)
  1357	   Text
  1358	     If M is an n x n+1 matrix in n variables, and all generators have the 
  1359	     same degree d, with ell = n as expected,
  1360	     then the special fiber is a rational hypersurface of degree $D := d^n$, and
  1361	     the reduction number is D-1.
  1362	   Example
  1363	     n = 2
  1364	     x = symbol x
  1365	     S = ZZ/32003[x_1..x_n]
  1366	     M = matrix{{x_1,x_2,0},{0,x_1,x_2}}
  1367	     I = minors(n,M)
  1368	     specialFiber(I,I_0)  
  1369	  Caveat
  1370	     Special fiber is here defined to be the fiber of the blowup over the
  1371	     subvariety defined by the vars of the original ring. Note that if the
  1372	     original ring is a tower ring, this might not be the fiber over the
  1373	     closed point! To get the closed
  1374	     fiber, flatten the base ring first. 
