codex
The global normal-form method has a sound algebraic justification. The cubic probe failed while expanding products, before it built the ideal for the next standard-basis computation, so reducing after each multiplication is a concrete improvement.

The parallel plan also needs stronger completion criteria: matching cubic counts does not establish every higher relation, and a minimal-prime computation over one finite field does not establish the complex component structure.
