   451	Key
   452	  MultigradedImplicitization
   453	Headline
   454	  Package for levaraging multigradings to solve implicitization problems
   455	Description
   456	  Text
   457	    The MultigradedImplicitization package provides methods for computing the maximal $\mathbb{Z}^k$ grading in which the 
   458	    kernel of a polynomial map $F$ is homogeneous and exploiting it to find generators of $\ker(F)$. This package is
   459	    particularly useful for problems from algebraic statistics which often involve highly structured maps $F$ which are
   460	    often naturally homogeneous in a larger multigrading than the standard $\mathbb{Z}$-multigrading given by total degree.
   461	    For more information on this approach see the following:
   462	  Text
   463	    References:
   464	
   465	    [1] Cummings, J., & Hollering , B. (2023). Computing Implicitizations of Multi-Graded Polynomial Maps. arXiv preprint arXiv:2311.07678.
   466	
   467	    [2] Cummings, J., & Hauenstein, J. (2023). Multi-graded Macaulay Dual Spaces. arXiv preprint arXiv:2310.11587.
   468	
   469	    [3] Cummings, J., Hollering, B., & Manon, C. (2024). Invariants for level-1 phylogenetic networks under the cavendar-farris-neyman model. Advances in Applied Mathematics, 153, 102633.
