    32	
    33	## 3. msolve failure, precisely
    34	esz is the monomial hash-table capacity; at doubling the code reallocates esz*evl*sizeof(exp_t) bytes for exponents (evl about 32 for 31 variables), plus the hd array and the column map, while the old block stays mapped [F compute-flags.md:30-40]. At esz=2^28 that is about 16 GiB (16-bit exponents [I], unverified: no source in tree) to 32 GiB for exponents alone. The trigger is the degree-7 round with 407,116 pairs. `-m N` caps pairs per matrix; the table still receives every monomial. `-u` drops stale monomials but the same step reaches the same esz [F u.log]. F4 option `-l 1` vs `2` changes linear algebra, not the table. Truncating the input is unsound for an elimination. Conclusion: msolve is not the tool.
